cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below, together with the original paper."
title: "Intraday Periodicity and Volatility Persistence, Revisited: A Replication and Extension of Andersen & Bollerslev (1997)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Garg
    given-names: Saksham
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-05
license: MIT
keywords:
  - intraday seasonality
  - volatility
  - GARCH
  - flexible Fourier form
  - replication
  - high-frequency finance
abstract: >-
  Replication of Andersen & Bollerslev (1997) on EUR/USD (2004-2025), S&P 500
  (2010-2025) and BTC/USDT (2018-2025) with free data, a zero-robust Poisson
  pseudo-ML estimator of the intraday periodic component, rolling-window
  robustness, and strict walk-forward out-of-sample tests of volatility
  forecasts and intraday trading rules.
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Andersen
        given-names: Torben G.
      - family-names: Bollerslev
        given-names: Tim
    title: "Intraday periodicity and volatility persistence in financial markets"
    journal: "Journal of Empirical Finance"
    volume: 4
    issue: "2-3"
    start: 115
    end: 158
    year: 1997
    doi: "10.1016/S0927-5398(97)00004-2"
